    {"id": "gateway.yolo", "class": "A", "ui": "yes", "applies": "per_field", "note": "The YOLO section (#444); each value says when it applies and which variable wins."},
    {"id": "gateway.progress", "class": "B", "ui": "no", "applies": "restart", "note": "Progress reports in a YOLO window (ADR 0014, #451); no Issue yet. B: an automatic continue starts a model turn (cost), so raising it is confirmed."},
    {"id": "gateway.run_checks", "class": "C", "ui": "no", "applies": "restart", "reason": "loosening", "issue": "#167", "note": "The verification runner, ADR 0019 phases 0-1: absent or {} = off (no tool registered); {\"phase\": 1} turns it on at the next start. Its rule is Ask by default; a saved Always is effective only on a verified macOS sandbox host (else read as Ask). stira doctor says how it would be contained."},
    {"id": "gateway.autonomy", "class": "C", "ui": "no", "applies": "restart", "reason": "loosening", "issue": "#296", "note": "ADR 0011 stage C (W4): {\"stage_c\": true} registers the goal-grant control plane at the next start (default off: no route, no file, no thread). run_checks_unattended (default true) counts only on a verified os_sandbox host. allow_browser_confirm (default false) accepts the weaker browser confirmation; otherwise issue / resume / verify need STIRA_YOLO_HOST_CONFIRM (dialog / command). W5: stage_c_exec (default false; needs stage_c) adds the goal iteration executor: a person's Run one iteration press runs exactly one iteration in the session grant:<id> (permits per model / tool call, budget reservations, the user verifies); iteration_wall_sec (60-3600, default 600) bounds one iteration. W6c: claim_stale_sec (60-86400, default 1800) is after how long an unverified completion claim is shown as still waiting for you (display only: no timer, no action). W6d: heartbeat_start (default false; needs stage_c_exec and a running scheduler) lets a grant issued with its own heartbeat_start flag (host-confirmed at issue) be started by the scheduler's model-free grant_tick, at most one iteration per wake through the same step as a press; tick_min_spacing_sec (30-86400, default 300) is the shortest time from the grant's issue, from an iteration's end and from the grant's last resume to a heartbeat-started one. Off: no executor, no route, no thread."},
    {"id": "gateway.handoff_inject", "class": "A", "ui": "no", "applies": "restart", "note": "Handoff notes (docs/handoff.md): the handoff_write / handoff_read tools and the newest note in the recalled part; on by default, no note = no section. The settings page does not edit it yet."},
    {"id": "gateway.handoff_max_tokens", "class": "A", "ui": "no", "applies": "restart", "note": "The largest note shown (100-1500, default 400, a conservative estimate); a larger one is left out whole."},
    {"id": "gateway.handoff_max_age_hours", "class": "A", "ui": "no", "applies": "restart", "note": "An older note is not shown (1-720, default 72)."},
    {"id": "gateway.task_models", "class": "A", "ui": "partial", "applies": "restart", "note": "Model per task (docs/task-models.md): shown read-only under Output limit and cost; changed in the file or with STIRA_TASK_MODEL_<TASK>. Empty = every task on the chat model."},
    {"id": "gateway.token_prices", "class": "A", "ui": "no", "applies": "restart", "issue": "#451", "note": "Token unit prices per model id (USD per million tokens; input and output required, cache_read / cache_write optional). Read at start-up; only a model with an entry gets an estimated cost on the activity board and the chat page. Stira ships no price data. The settings page does not edit it yet."},
    {"id": "gateway.delegation", "class": "A", "ui": "yes", "applies": "next_turn", "note": "Sub-agents (delegate), ADR 0016 phase 1 (#486): on / off and three caps; read at every turn and every call. Each call is still a person's card."},
    {"id": "gateway.agent_jobs", "class": "A", "ui": "yes", "applies": "restart", "note": "Scheduled agent jobs, ADR 0021 S2 (#239): on / off (default off) and the daily token pool agent_daily_token_budget (50,000). Read at start; jobs come up paused after every start."},

